   Tokyo, JAPAN, JUN 29-30, 2013},
Organization = {TU Bergakademie Freiberg; Tianjin Univ Finance Econ, Tourism Dept;
   Waseda Univ; German Acad Exchange Serv Fdn; IMRE Alumni Network},
Abstract = {City Square is an important part in modern cities, thus, the design of
   city square should follow the principles of humanity. The structure of
   squares will be a strong vitality as long as going by psychological
   researches. In this paper, the authors firstly discuss environmental
   factors destroying a good mood, which are weather, population density,
   and noise; and then use the Space Bubble Theory to analyze the spatial
   variation of Chinese people. Based on boundary effects, the authors
   conclude that the edge area is the best place people like to go. At the
   end of the paper, the authors provide several suggestions for city
   squares' design and urban environmental construction based on
   environmental psychology theories.},
