   Inst Architects; Hong Kong Institut Engineers; Hong Kong Inst Surveyors;
   HKSTS; IUE; JSCE; RICS; Urban Planning Soc China; China Civil Engn Soc;
   Hong Kong Inst Util Specialists},
Abstract = {Diesel oil-water emulsion fuel (water in-oil type) in this experiment is
   obtained by mixing Diesel Oil (DO) and water. The laboratory
   experimental project is using 10\% water mixed with Diesel Oil (DO).
   These components are mixed in mechanical mixer controlled, to produce
   blending fuel. During the blending process the special additives to make
   oil surrounds the water droplet to prevent the water from separating out
   of the mixture. The encapsulation size in 20-30 micrometer prevents the
   water from contacting any metal engine parts, thereby allowing the fuel
   to perform in a similar fashion to conventional diesel. The experiment
   was conducted with diesel engine set-up at 2000 rpm with variable of
   engine load. Measurement of engine emissions parameters at different
   load conditions have generally indicated reduce in engine CO, NO and SO2
   emission as compared to base diesel oil.},
