   VANCOUVER, CANADA, SEP 21-25, 1998},
Organization = {Int Assoc Engn Geol \& Environm},
Abstract = {In the last few years the Geological Survey of the Regione Lombardia has
   been carrying out specific projects on the prevention of natural hazards
   and in particular on risk generated by unstable slopes in urban areas. A
   database linked with a GIS was designed in order to archive, analyse and
   display data concerning instability processes. The database was tested
   with a data set already available for the Sondrio Province, which also
   included advice for devising and implementing measures for risk
   mitigation, monitoring systems, and management of emergency situations.
   The GIS database provides all the information under the same
   environment, allowing the creation of hazard and risk maps, territorial
   planning maps and maps of risk scenarios and connected emergency plans.},
