Note = {5th International Conference on Urban Regeneration and Sustainability
   (The Sustainable City), Skiathos Isl, GREECE, SEP 24-26, 2008},
Organization = {Univ Thessaly; Wessex Inst Technol; Univ Siena; WIT Transact Ecol \&
   Environm},
Abstract = {Half the world's population now lives in urban areas. Urbanisation has
   been a rapid process and virtually all the forecast population growth in
   coming years will take place in urban areas in less developed countries.
   Research into urbanisation at Arup has been undertaken as part of an
   initiative to look at Drivers of Change - an ongoing programme exploring
   issues most likely to have a major impact upon society. There is clear
   evidence that urbanisation can play a positive role in social and
   economic development. By concentrating half the world's population on
   less than 3\% of its land area, urban settlements give sustainability a
   better chance. However, cities also draw together many of the world's
   major environmental problems. It is important to understand the
   negatives associated with urbanisation and see these in terms of
   opportunities and chances to do things differently in the future.},
