Note = {International Symposium on Social Sciences, Arts and Humanities
   (SYSSARM), Bali, INDONESIA, SEP 29-OCT 01, 2015},
Abstract = {The significance of patriotic songs has become one of the essences in
   promoting unity in many regions, especially in Malaysia. This study is
   conducted to examine the significance of words and lyrics consisted in
   patriotic songs in Najib Razak's terms as the Prime Minister of Malaysia
   by employing a semantic analysis method. Throughout his two terms, the
   perception of the public has been shaped and changed rigorously through
   the means of entertainment, with an aim to unite and educate the public
   towards the nation's vision and mission, particularly in regards to the
   concept of 1Malaysia. Thus, this study seeks to highlight the importance
   of lyrics and words used in patriotic songs-whether the messages,
   composed by songwriters-are accepted or rejected by the listeners. In
   addition, this study looks into the traits of psychology and the history
   of Malaysia in terms of songs to influence people's hearts and minds,
   predominantly in Malaysia's multiethnic society, in which it reflects
   public preferences of patriotic songs. Therefore, this study examines
   ten (10) songs that are thoroughly selected from the year 2008 until
   2013 (within Najib Razak's terms as prime minister), and simultaneously
   evaluating the acceptance of propagated agendas through patriotic songs.
   Finally, the results of this research can be used as a reference for
   songwriters to produce better, improved patriotic songs that could
   foster unity among multiethnic Malaysians.},
