Abstract = {The papers in the session ``Food Culture and Consumer Response,{''} show
   how important people's values, beliefs, aspirations and social context
   are to their dietary health. They also reveal several tensions that
   shape consumer responses to healthy food. This essay discusses the
   paradoxical nature of eating habits in general, and describes three
   paradoxes related specifically to the challenges of providing food for
   health in the 21st century: pleasure/health, technology/nature,
   innovation/nostalgia.},
