   NEWPORT, RI, JUN 15-19, 1996},
Organization = {Interdisciplinary Environm Assoc},
Abstract = {This paper describes a research project designed to inform decisions on
   sustainable settlement patterns. The project has been submitted to the
   engineering and Physical Sciences Research Council who have shortlisted
   the proposal for funding to begin in 1997.
   The proposal is to carry out research on the energy consumed and CO2
   omitted by alternative retail outlets in the distribution of the same
   goods. This will help the debate about the relative sustainability of
   retail formats in order that urban planners can make rational decisions
   about future development patterns. A limited range of goods will be
   investigated initially with the intention of developing a research
   methodology that can then be applied to other types of goods and indeed
   other sectors such as leisure.},
