Abstract = {In order to apply a distributed model to sewer systems in Japan, a
   data-conversion system was constructed in which existing sewer ledger
   data were converted to a network data file for the distributed model.
   This system has a function for inputting land use data to the network
   data file. Then a distributed model was applied to investigate
   stormwater runoff and non-point pollution load analysis considering
   impervious surface characteristics. Simulation results show that
   considering impervious surface characteristics in the analysis is
   effective to explain the dynamic changes of stormwater and non-point
   pollution runoff.},
