   Antalya, TURKEY, APR 22-25, 2010},
Abstract = {The goal of the experiment was to expose changes in viewing distance
   while evaluating and reporting 48 affective ( IAPS) pictures. The
   experiment consisted of 25 female students. Pictures appeared on the
   screen for 20 secs in random order. After reporting the SAM, the
   participant orally reported to the experimenter what she saw, what had
   happened, and what was going to happen in the picture. Results indicated
   that subjects took the most distance from positive pictures and
   approached negative pictures, which was in contradiction with earlier
   studies. The effect of the reporting phase given to the subjects is
   discussed. (C) 2010 Elsevier Ltd. All rights reserved.},
